PN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Miami tops Virginia Tech, to face Wake Forest in ACC title game","description":"Miami will play Wake Forest in the ACC title game on Dec. 5 after both teams won on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-22T04:46:52.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50558418/miami-tops-virginia-tech-face-wake-forest-acc-title-game","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Betting buzz: Big Ten's odds of national champion four-peat getting slim","description":"Losses by UCLA, Indiana and Ohio State make the Big Ten's chances of winning the national championship this season a long shot.","published":"2026-11-22T04:06:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/49921234/college-football-betting-buzz-odds-updates-line-moves-spreads","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5145410/chris-cole","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Cole_(linebacker)"},"pick":{"pick":9,"round":1,"team":"TB","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Chris Cole (linebacker)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Cole_(linebacker)","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-22T04:17:55Z","intro":"Christopher Cole (born October 3, 2005) is an American college football linebacker for the Georgia Bulldogs.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Cole attended Salem High School in Salem, Virginia. As a junior, he recorded 76 tackles and 11 tackles-for-loss. A four-star recruit and one of the top-rated players in the state of Virginia, Cole committed to play college football at the University of Georgia over offers from Miami, Penn State, and Tennessee."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman, Cole totaled 16 tackles and two fumble recoveries, being named to the SEC All-Freshman Team. Entering the 2025 season, he was expected to earn a bigger role in the Bulldogs defense. Cole finished the season recording 60 tackles and 4.5 sacks.Against Oklahoma in 2026, he recorded a sack and two fumble recoveries, returning one 85 yards for a touchdown in a 41–13 victory. Cole was named SEC Defensive Player of the Week for his performance. He was named a Butkus Award semifinalist in October."}]}}